From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] tty: serial: samsung: build without ARCH_EXYNOS

The one Kconfig dependency the lynx GKI needs relaxed. gs201's console
UART is a Samsung UART, and earlycon=exynos4210 (gs201.dtsi bootargs) is
provided only by the built-in samsung_tty driver. Upstream it depends on
ARCH_EXYNOS, but enabling ARCH_EXYNOS would also build upstream's Exynos
clock, pinctrl, PMU and MCT drivers into the GKI, which collide with the
gs201 vendor modules that provide those. AOSP's GKI drops the same
dependency line for the same reason; this is that hunk.
---
diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/Kconfig b/drivers/tty/serial/Kconfig
index cf7dba473..297f07674 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/Kconfig
@@ -219,7 +219,6 @@ config SERIAL_CLPS711X_CONSOLE
 
 config SERIAL_SAMSUNG
 	tristate "Samsung SoC serial support"
-	depends on PLAT_SAMSUNG || ARCH_S5PV210 || ARCH_EXYNOS || ARCH_APPLE || ARCH_ARTPEC || COMPILE_TEST
 	select SERIAL_CORE
 	help
 	  Support for the on-chip UARTs on the Samsung
